I think you're right - we need to include some ID so we can pair up the request with the response. I think that library you found is overkill - it has configuration for all sorts including setting the header on the response which we don't want. Have a look at [this comment](https://github.com/expressjs/morgan/issues/40#issuecomment-62004614) for a simple way to do the same thing.

And yes, let's get rid of the date at the same time.

I think it's probably also worth changing the log configuration so we don't get so many empty fields on the request side. What about this...

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  req.id = uuid.v4();
  next();
});
morgan.token('id', req => req.id);
app.use(morgan('REQ :id :remote-addr :remote-user :method :url HTTP/:http-version', {immediate: true}));
app.use(morgan('RES :id :remote-addr :remote-user :method :url HTTP/:http-version :status :res[content-length] :response-time ms'));
```

That adds the ID, removes the date, and uses a consistent format between request and response logging.

What do you think?

